<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peña Amaya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peña Amaya is a flat-topped mountain in the north of the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgos">Burgos</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, the site of an ancient hill fort of the Cantabri. It remained an important stronghold in Roman and Visigothic times and was captured by the Visigothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liuvigild">Leovigild</a> in 574. After the Muslim conquest it was resettled in 860 for the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> by Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rodrigo-of-castile">Rodrigo of Castile</a>.</p></div>
